'''Masori armour''' is a set of [[ranged]] armour requiring level 80 [[Ranged]] and 30 [[Defence]] to equip. The armour belonged to the Masori clan, who were powerful ranged weapon-wielders active around the time of the [[Kharidian–Zarosian War]] and were known for defending people from bandits who sought to take advantage of the wartime chaos.{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/tombs-of-amascut?oldschool=1|title=Tombs of Amascut|newsdate=24 August 2022|quote=The Masori were powerful ranged weapon wielders active during an ancient Kharidian war. They defended ordinary people from the violent thieves and murderers who sought to take advantage of the wartime chaos. This mighty clan has long since disbanded, but their weapons can still be found in the palaces of wealthy Menaphites, and among the treasures of long-dead Pharaohs.}} Their armour can only be obtained as rare drops from the [[Tombs of Amascut]].

It is the best ranged armour in the game, surpassing [[Armadyl armour]] in terms of ranged attack bonuses and does not provide a penalty to melee accuracy like Armadyl armour does. The Masori armour can also be upgraded into a fortified variant with [[Armadyl plate]]s, increasing the Defence level required to equip it to 80, offering increased defensive bonuses and a +1 [[prayer bonus]]. This fortified version provides the highest magic defence bonus of all armour in the game, surpassing other Ranged armour sets such as [[Karil the Tainted's equipment|Karil's]] or Armadyl. Fortifying the armour requires level 90 [[Crafting]].

Completing the Tombs of Amascut with a raid level of at least 350 and without dying will reward the [[Masori crafting kit]]. This kit can be combined with an [[Ava's assembler]] to create the [[Masori assembler]], which has the same function as the regular assembler but matches the style of Masori armour. A [[Masori assembler max cape]] can similarly be created by either combining the kit with an [[assembler max cape]] or by combining a Masori assembler with a regular [[max cape]].

